# Shell scripts must check out with LF even on Windows (core.autocrlf=true):
# a CRLF shebang line makes macOS and Linux reject the file with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Bundled media (the chime, and the ARCH §5 fallback clips and images) must
# never be line-ending translated — a single rewritten byte is a corrupt file.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# api/fixtures/worksheet.pdf is a hand-written, all-ASCII PDF: it holds no NUL
# byte, so git's auto-detection calls it *text* and autocrlf=true would rewrite
# every LF on checkout — which shifts the byte offsets its xref table records
# and yields "Broken xref table". Force it binary.
*.pdf binary
